# TypeScript

- Keep `strict` on. Do not add unjustified `any`.
- Prefer inferred types from Zod schemas over handwritten duplicates.
- Use type-only imports when importing only types.
- Avoid unnecessary assertions. Handle null with explicit checks.
- Name files and exports for the concept they represent (`create-task.use-case.ts`).
- Do not use deprecated `moduleResolution` values (`node` / `node10`) or `baseUrl`.
- Bundled apps (`apps/web`, `@repo/ui`): `module` `preserve` + `moduleResolution` `bundler`.
- Node CJS emit (`apps/api`, `@repo/contracts`): `module` `commonjs` + `moduleResolution` `bundler` (TypeScript 6 upgrade path). Do not add `ignoreDeprecations` to silence TS 6/7 deprecations.
